Applies to these skill directories in agent/skills/, copied 2026-09-15 from
pstack/skills at be432a96ed36:

  blast-radius                      (modified -- see below)
  create-verification-skill         (heavily ported -- see below; incl.
                                     references/feature-map-example/)
  interrogate                       (ported -- see below; incl.
                                     references/rubric.md, reviewer-prompt.md,
                                     lead-judgment.md, code-quality-review.md)
  maintain-verification-skill       (heavily ported -- see below)
  principle-boundary-discipline     (vendored so typescript-best-practices's
                                     boundary-validation rule can cite it)
  principle-type-system-discipline
  typescript-best-practices         (incl. references/patterns.md)
  unslop

All of them ship `disable-model-invocation: true` upstream and keep it, so they
add nothing to the always-loaded skill index and are reachable only as
`/skill:<name>` or `skill://<name>`. The rest of pstack is deliberately not
vendored: poteto-mode's tree is ~327K and hard-wires Cursor built-ins,
cursor-team-kit, `subagent_type` spawns and cursor model slugs, and the other 21
principle leaves restate rules the omp system prompt already carries -- the two
vendored above are the exceptions with teeth.

Modified per skill:

- blast-radius: lines 11, 33, 36 and 38 referenced pstack's `how`, `why` and
  `arena` skills, none vendored here. They now describe the split inline
  (a `task`/`scout` explainer dispatch for what the code does) and point at
  plain `git blame`/`git log`/PR archaeology and a `task` fan-out across model
  families. `typescript-best-practices` had its frontmatter `paths:` key
  renamed to omp's `globs:`, its "type-system-discipline" reference fixed to
  the vendored `principle-type-system-discipline`, and its
  "boundary-discipline" reference fixed to the vendored
  `principle-boundary-discipline`. Nothing else changed in these two, the
  principle leaves, or unslop.
- create-verification-skill / maintain-verification-skill: heavily rewritten for
  omp. Generated verify skills target `.omp/skills/verify-<app>/` (omp's native
  project skill root, confirmed by nonce probe against the shipped binary);
  server lifecycle is the `hub` tool (`start` with a `ready` probe, `logs`,
  `ps`, `stop`) instead of tmux or `scripts`; web driving is the `eval` browser
  facade; CLI/TUI driving is `hub` PTY `send`; PRs and CI are the `github`
  device (`pr_create`, `run_watch`); the read-only per-feature subagent became
  one `task` batch of `scout` items; `/create-skill` and `/loop` references
  deleted.
- interrogate: Step 3 rewritten for omp. The four Cursor reviewer models became
  one `task` batch across four agent/family vehicles: `reviewer` (`@critic`,
  OpenAI), `security-reviewer` (`@sentinel`, GLM), `interrogator` (`@plan`,
  Anthropic), `task` (`@task`, DeepSeek). Upstream's `subagent_type`,
  per-item `model:` slugs, slug-fallback paragraph and `pstack-models.mdc` hook
  deleted; `task.agentModelOverrides` named as the omp equivalent. Scope step
  gained `pr://<N>/diff` and packaging to `local://interrogate-package.md`.
  references/lead-judgment.md and references/code-quality-review.md are
  upstream byte-identical; rubric and reviewer-prompt have tool-name edits only.
  Companion file original to this repository: agent/agents/interrogator.md (the
  Anthropic arm; read-only tools `read`, `grep`, `glob`, `lsp`).

Upstream ships its license at pstack/LICENSE rather than inside each skill
directory, so it is reproduced here instead of vendored alongside the skills.

